  ! Take over the repository /srv/demo-foreign as a local stack folder?                                                 
                                                                                                                        
  Yes makes the changes listed below.                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
    folder: /srv/demo-foreign                                                                                           
    case: local (a repository without a remote, deployed as it is)                                                      
                                                                                                                        
  Foreign project                                                                                                       
    project: legacy-blog                                                                                                
    compose files (labels): /srv/demo-foreign/compose.yaml                                                              
    env files (labels): /srv/demo-foreign/.env                                                                          
                                                                                                                        
  Warning                                                                                                               
    project name: the running containers belong to legacy-blog, a deploy would use blog                                 
    compose files: the running containers use /srv/demo-foreign/compose.yaml, a deploy would pass /srv/demo-            
    foreign/compose.yml                                                                                                 
    env files: the running containers use /srv/demo-foreign/.env, a deploy would pass -                                 
    The first deploy would create new containers instead of taking over the running ones.                               
                                                                                                                        
    owner: root, group: root, mode: 0755                                                                                
    the service can write it: yes                                                                                       
    permissions are set: no                                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
  Stacks (1)                                                                                                            
    legacy-blog (folder .)                                                                                              
      works: deploy                                                                                                     
      does not work: backup                                                                                             
                                                                                                                        
  Changes after yes                                                                                                     
    The repository is taken over as a local stack folder.                                                               
    No permission changes: the service can write already.                                                               
    The folder is added to the systemd drop-in of the service, which restarts once.                                     
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
